# TypeScript Client Quality

- Enable strict TypeScript checks; do not use `any`.
- Keep browser/protocol details out of shared TIR models.
- Validate untrusted data at process and protocol boundaries.
- Prefer discriminated unions and exhaustive `never` checks.
- Use `unknown` in catch clauses and preserve error causes.
- Pass cancellation signals through asynchronous operations.
- Keep side effects explicit and isolate transport from pure transformations.
- Preserve source ordering; do not add timestamps or random IDs to core TIR.
- Add focused tests for serialization and boundary failures.
- Add dependencies only for current, demonstrated needs.
